From d06b61343dd0b8d56df4d25ee595e92414331ea2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redgrave961 <214504937+Redgrave961@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:23:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sceNpTrophy: the title's real trophy set, firmware error
 codes and layouts

The trophy set is read from the title's TROPHY.TRP: the booted application's
TROPDIR (an installed disc-game update) first, then the disc, and the
TROP_<language>.SFM text (else TROP.SFM), as RPCS3 does. GetGameInfo,
GetTrophyInfo, GetTrophyUnlockState, GetGameProgress, UnlockTrophy (with the
platinum rule: unlocked with the last trophy linked to it) and
GetRequiredDiskSpace (pack size minus header and entry table) answer from it.
Every guest struct is written big-endian at its real offsets; the old code
wrote a fabricated 32-trophy set in host byte order, which titles read as
0x20000000 trophies.

Error codes, the 1024-byte description fields, GameDetails' reserved tail,
the processing status values and the context/handle validation are the
firmware's (they were a made-up 0x805516xx range). Registration calls the
status callback with INSTALLED or NOT_INSTALLED, honours a negative return,
then queues SETUP/PROGRESS/FINALIZE/COMPLETE through sysutil. Unlock times
are CellRtc ticks.

trophy_files.c/.h (TRP and SFM reader) is from the inFAMOUS 2 port
(SamiEnazi/infamous2-port, MIT), with the full 1024-byte detail and the
title-detail text added and the header sizes kept for the space query.

cellFs maps /dev_hdd0 to $PS3_HDD0_ROOT like sys_fs and ppu_fs do;
ps3_sysutil_language() exposes the system language to other modules.

The trophy tests are rewritten for this behaviour with a generated pack
fixture; they are POSIX-only and were not run on this Windows host.
